      "itemIdentifier": "ogc.model.cross-domain.prov",
      "name": "PROV",
      "abstract": "Provenance Ontology",
      "highlighted": true,
      "status": "stable",
      "dateTimeAddition": "2023-09-18T00:00:00Z",
      "itemClass": "model",
      "register": "ogc-incubator",
      "version": "1.0",
      "dateOfLastChange": "2026-09-16",
      "link": "https://github.com/ogcincubator/cross-domain-model",
      "dependsOn": null,
      "shaclShapes": [
        {
          "prof:hasArtifact": [
            "https://ogcincubator.github.io/cross-domain-model/_sources/prov/shapes.shacl"
          ],
          "rdfs:seeAlso": "bblocks://ogc.model.cross-domain.prov",
          "prof:hasRole": "role:validation",
          "dct:format": "text/turtle",
          "dct:conformsTo": "shacl:"
        }
      ],
      "shaclClosures": [],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "PROV-O Specification",
          "link": "https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-o/"
        }
      ],
      "scope": "dev",
      "tags": [
        "PROV"
      ],
      "ontology": {
        "prof:hasArtifact": "https://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o",
        "prof:hasRole": "role:specification",
        "dct:format": "text/turtle",
        "dct:conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"
      },
      "remoteCacheDir": "https://ogcincubator.github.io/cross-domain-model/build/annotated/model/cross-domain/prov/remote_cache/",
      "sourceFiles": "https://ogcincubator.github.io/cross-domain-model/_sources/prov/",
      "validationPassed": true,
      "testOutputs": "https://github.com/ogcincubator/cross-domain-model/blob/master/build/tests/model/cross-domain/prov/",
      "transforms": [
        {
          "id": "entail",
          "description": "Applies RDFS entailment (PROV-O's own rdfs:domain/rdfs:range axioms) to a PROV\nTurtle graph, materializing the rdf:type statements this block's shapes.shacl\ndoes not require locally so that every object-property value -- blank node or\nby-reference IRI alike -- ends up explicitly typed. The output is validated\nagainst the strict profile, whose shapes require that typing unconditionally.\n",
          "type": "python",
          "inputs": {
            "mediaTypes": [
              {
                "mimeType": "text/turtle",
                "label": "RDF/Turtle",
                "defaultExtension": "ttl"
              }
            ]
          },
          "outputs": {
            "mediaTypes": [
              {
                "mimeType": "text/turtle",
                "label": "RDF/Turtle",
                "defaultExtension": "ttl"
              }
            ],
            "profiles": [
              "bblocks://ogc.model.cross-domain.prov-strict"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {
            "dependencies": {
              "pip": "pyshacl>=0.25"
            }
          },
          "ref": "https://ogcincubator.github.io/cross-domain-model/_sources/prov/transforms/entail.py",
          "code": "\"\"\"\nMaterializes the rdf:type triples that PROV-O's own rdfs:domain/rdfs:range axioms imply\nbut that this block's shapes.shacl deliberately does not require locally (see that\nfile's header comment on the open-world, by-reference-typing relaxation).\n\nGiven a Turtle graph valid against ../shapes.shacl (which only checks sh:class on\nblank-node values), this applies RDFS entailment -- via pySHACL's own `inference`\noption, i.e. the SHACL \"entailment regime\" pySHACL's shapes-graph validation shapes\nname but never itself executes for the data graph (see shapes.shacl's header for why\nthis had been left undone until now) -- against the graph merged with the live PROV-O\nontology, then keeps only the original triples plus any newly-entailed prov:* rdf:type\nstatements about nodes already present in the input. The result is validated (see\ntransforms.yaml's `outputs.profiles`) against ../../prov-strict, whose shapes require\nsh:class for every value described in the graph, exempting only values with no\noutgoing triples of their own. This entailment step matters even so: it types every\nPROV object-property value from the property assertion alone, regardless of local\ndescription, so a value that would otherwise only pass via that \"not described\"\nexemption ends up genuinely, explicitly typed instead.\n\"\"\"\nimport urllib.request\n\nimport pyshacl\nimport rdflib\nfrom rdflib import RDF, Namespace, URIRef, BNode\n\nPROV = Namespace(\"http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#\")\nPROV_O_URL = \"https://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#\"\n\ndata_graph = rdflib.Graph()\ndata_graph.parse(data=input_data, format=\"turtle\")\n\noriginal_triples = set(data_graph)\noriginal_nodes = {\n    term for triple in original_triples for term in (triple[0], triple[2])\n    if isinstance(term, (URIRef, BNode))\n}\n\nwith urllib.request.urlopen(\n    urllib.request.Request(PROV_O_URL, headers={\"Accept\": \"text/turtle\"})\n) as resp:\n    ontology_ttl = resp.read()\n\nworking_graph = rdflib.Graph()\nfor triple in original_triples:\n    working_graph.add(triple)\nworking_graph.parse(data=ontology_ttl, format=\"turtle\")\n\n# inference='rdfs' is pySHACL's RDFS entailment regime; inplace=True materializes the\n# inferred triples directly into working_graph instead of only reporting on them.\npyshacl.validate(data_graph=working_graph, shacl_graph=None, inference=\"rdfs\",\n                  inplace=True, advanced=True)\n\nresult_graph = rdflib.Graph()\nfor prefix, namespace in data_graph.namespaces():\n    result_graph.bind(prefix, namespace, override=True)\nfor triple in original_triples:\n    result_graph.add(triple)\nfor node in original_nodes:\n    for entailed_type in working_graph.objects(node, RDF.type):\n        if str(entailed_type).startswith(str(PROV)):\n            result_graph.add((node, RDF.type, entailed_type))\n\noutput_data = result_graph.serialize(format=\"turtle\")\n"
        }
      ],
      "documentation": {
        "markdown": {
          "mediatype": "text/markdown",
          "url": "https://ogcincubator.github.io/cross-domain-model/build/generateddocs/markdown/model/cross-domain/prov/index.md"
        },
